Aircraft noise is measured by
(A) L_{\text{epn}}
(B) L_{\text{eq}}
(C) L_{10} (18hrs) index
(D) Decibel ENGINEERING MECHANICS (Q71–85)

The arms of a common balance are of unequal length, but the beam remains horizontal when the pans are not loaded. If W_1 and W_2 are the measured weights of a body when placed in left and right pans respectively, the correct weight is
(A) \frac{W_1+W_2}{2}
(B) \sqrt{W_1 W_2}
(C) \sqrt{W_1^2+W_2^2}
(D) \frac{2W_1W_2}{W_1+W_2}

A force P_1 acting on a body along an inclined plane upward is just enough to drag the body upward. The plane is rough, inclined at angle \theta. If the force is reduced to P_2 (same direction), the body is about to slip down. The weight of the body is
(A) \frac{P_1+P_2}{2}\sin\theta
(B) \frac{P_1+P_2}{2\tan\theta}
(C) \frac{P_1+P_2}{2\cos\theta}
(D) \frac{P_1+P_2}{2}\cos\theta

[Diagram] D is the centre of the circular base of a right circular solid cone ABC, vertical angle 60^\circ. The largest possible sphere is scooped out. The centre of gravity of the remaining solid lies at G. Find AG : GD.
(A) \frac{47}{11}
(B) \frac{48}{11}
(C) \frac{49}{11}
(D) \frac{50}{11}

Two particles of masses 5\text{ kg} and 10\text{ kg} are moving with speed 2\text{ m/s} in +x direction and +y direction respectively. After collision, they stick together. The velocity of the combined mass is
(A) \frac{2\sqrt{2}}{3}\text{ m/s}
(B) \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}\text{ m/s}
(C) 2\sqrt{3}\text{ m/s}
(D) 3\sqrt{2}\text{ m/s}

The ratio of polar moments of inertia of a circular lamina and a square lamina having the same area is
(A) \frac{3}{\pi}
(B) \frac{3}{2\pi}
(C) \frac{4}{\pi}
(D) \frac{5}{4\pi}

Two equal balls P and Q lie in contact in a smooth horizontal circular groove. They are projected along the groove and collide after time t. The second impact will take place after a further interval of (e = coefficient of restitution)
(A) \frac{2t}{e}
(B) \frac{t}{e}
(C) \frac{t}{2e}
(D) \frac{t}{3e}

A long slender bar of uniform cross‑section B \times H is acted upon by an axial compressive force. Ends behave as pin‑jointed when buckling in plane normal to x‑axis, and as built‑in when buckling in plane normal to y‑axis. If axial load capacity (buckling) is same in both modes, the ratio B/H is
(A) \frac{1}{2}
(B) \frac{1}{4}
(C) \frac{1}{8}
(D) \frac{1}{16}

A uniform cantilever beam AB of length l and flexural rigidity EI carries a distributed load varying from zero at fixed end to W per unit length at free end. The deflection at free end is
(A) \frac{1}{48}\frac{W l^4}{EI}
(B) \frac{1}{30}\frac{W l^4}{EI}
(C) \frac{1}{20}\frac{W l^4}{EI}
(D) \frac{11}{120}\frac{W l^4}{EI}

A beam has a square cross‑section with side x. At a section, the transverse shear force is S. The magnitude of shear stress at the top surface of the beam at that section is
(A) 1.5\frac{S}{x^2}
(B) \frac{S}{x^2}
(C) 0.5\frac{S}{x^2}
(D) zero

The ratio of equivalent length of a column having one end fixed and other end free to its actual length is
(A) 2
(B) \sqrt{2}
(C) \frac{1}{2}
(D) \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}

Total strain energy stored in a simply supported beam of span L and flexural rigidity EI, subjected to a concentrated load W at mid‑span, is
(A) \frac{1}{40}\frac{W^2 L^3}{EI}
(B) \frac{1}{60}\frac{W^2 L^3}{EI}
(C) \frac{1}{96}\frac{W^2 L^3}{EI}
(D) \frac{1}{120}\frac{W^2 L^3}{EI}

Two circular shafts of same material, same length L and same outside diameter D are subjected to torques producing the same maximum shear stress. First shaft is solid, second is hollow with inner diameter D/2. The ratio of total strain energy absorbed by first shaft to that by second shaft is
(A) \frac{4}{3}
(B) \frac{8}{7}
(C) \frac{15}{16}
(D) \frac{16}{15} ```
